  "note": "Lean defines the odd-m, prime-only versions of (5.6)/(5.38). Erratum: The book says the integrand of (1.28) is at most √(S₁S₂), but η₁ = 2 on [1/2,1] makes the integrand 4·Σ_m c_m Σ_n Λ(n)e(αmn) over the unweighted ranges of (1.29), so Cauchy–Schwarz gives 4√(S₁S₂); at x = 1015000, U = V = 100, W = 10⁴, α = 1/101 the integrand is 3.909·√(S₁S₂). (checked by `scripts/checks/eq_1_29.py`)."
